# Applies specifically to `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .` (build
# context is the repo ROOT — see backend/Dockerfile's own comment for
# why) — Docker's per-Dockerfile ignore-file convention
# (<dockerfile>.dockerignore), picked so this doesn't have to be one
# giant ignore file shared with the unrelated frontend build. Patterns
# are relative to the repo root, the actual build context.
.git/
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
backend/tests/
frontend/
data/processed/
*.md
